      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n---\n\nAcross `cli_test.cc`, `ft_scsi_test.cc`, and `updater_test.cc`, almost every single test case repeats the exact same 3–4 lines of setup boilerplate:\n\n```c\nauto transport \u003d std::make_unique\u003cFakeEcTransport\u003e();\nauto* fake \u003d transport.get();\nUsbDevice device \u003d MakeDevice(std::move(transport));\n\n```\n\n**Improvement:** You can eliminate dozens of lines of repetitive code by upgrading your `TEST` macros to `TEST_F` and using a GTest fixture. GTest will automatically run `SetUp()` before every test:\n\n```c\nclass CliTest : public ::testing::Test {\n protected:\n  void SetUp() override {\n    auto t \u003d std::make_unique\u003cFakeEcTransport\u003e();\n    fake_ \u003d t.get();\n    device_ \u003d std::make_unique\u003cUsbDevice\u003e(std::move(t));\n  }\n  \n  FakeEcTransport* fake_;\n  std::unique_ptr\u003cUsbDevice\u003e device_;\n};\n\n// Now tests are instantly 3 lines shorter:\nTEST_F(CliTest, SwitchToBootloader_Success) {\n  fake_-\u003eAddResponse(BuildEmptySuccessResponse());\n  auto result \u003d SwitchToBootloader(*device_, 0);\n  EXPECT_TRUE(result.has_value());\n}\n\n```",
