      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n----\n\nIn `ft_scsi_test.cc`, you have several verbose `Invoke` lambdas used to return values to functions expecting a `std::expected`.\n\n```c\nEXPECT_CALL(*mock, Send(_, _))\n    .WillOnce(Invoke([](auto, auto) -\u003e std::expected\u003cint, Error\u003e {\n      return testing::kUsbCbwSize;\n    }));\n\n```\n\n**Improvement:** Because `std::expected` allows implicit conversion from a valid value (or `std::unexpected`), GTest\u0027s `Return()` handles this natively. You can strip out the lambdas entirely:\n\n```c\nEXPECT_CALL(*mock, Send(_, _))\n    .WillOnce(Return(testing::kUsbCbwSize));\n\n// And for errors:\nEXPECT_CALL(*mock, Send(_, _))\n    .WillOnce(Return(std::unexpected(Error::kNoSuchDevice)));\n\n```",
