      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n-----\n\n\nIn `GetFlashProtection`, `SetFlashProtection`, and `GetBootVersion`, the code allocates `std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e` for fixed, small payload sizes (36 to 512 bytes).\n\n```c\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e dummy(kFlashWpBufferSize, 0);\nauto res \u003d ReceiveActionIn(..., dummy, ...);\n\n```\n\n**Improvement:** Heap allocations (`std::vector`) can be avoided for tiny, static command buffers. Switching to `std::array` keeps this entirely on the stack, which is faster and safer for low-level I/O tasks.\n\n```c\nstd::array\u003cuint8_t, kFlashWpBufferSize\u003e dummy{};\nauto res \u003d ReceiveActionIn(..., dummy, ...);\n\n```",
